# The one radius of the sum (and of the difference) of two BallVectors with 2-limb centers
# (milestone2.md, "BallVector": bv_add_radius_k): the radius lines of ball_add_2, with m, the
# largest magnitude of the leading limb of a center of the result, in place of one entry's |cz0|.
# Every operation is a rounding of a nondecreasing function of m on nonnegative values, so with m
# the largest |cz0| the result is the largest of the radii that ball_add_2 returns entry by entry.
# Its claim is what makes it a radius of every entry: by the bound of add_2_2 relative to the
# result, an entry whose exact center is s and computed center cz has |cz - s| <= U |cz| <=
# U (1 + u) |cz0| <= U (1 + u) m, with U = unit/(1 - unit), and a member of the exact sum is within
# rx + ry of s. (With the roundings of the listing, each of a nonnegative value, the radius is at
# least rx + ry + U (1 + u)^2 m; the claim keeps what the containment needs.)
kernel:        bv_add_radius_2
input:         m
input:         rx
input:         ry
output:        rz
requires:      nonneg m
requires:      nonneg rx
requires:      nonneg ry
ensures:       upper rz value=rx+ry+m*unit(add_2_2)/(1-unit(add_2_2))*(1+u)
min_precision: 3
source:        the radius lines of ball_add_2 (Milestone 1, second radius design), at the largest magnitude of a center of the result (milestone2.md, BallVector)
license:       algorithm and proof: MIT
status:        unverified

s  = add(rx, ry)
t  = fma(m, const up(unit(add_2_2)/(1-unit(add_2_2))*(1+u)), s)
rz = fma(t, const up((1+u)^3), const up((1+u)*((1+u)^2*eta+eta/2)+eta/(2*u)))
